<title>USA: U.N. okays 48th Iraq oil contract for 100,000 bbls.</title>
<headline>U.N. okays 48th Iraq oil contract for 100,000 bbls.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.N. overseers have approved a 48th oil contract for Iraq under terms of the oil-for-food accord, allowing a spot deal for 100,000 barrels, a U.N. official said Friday.</p>
<p>The buyer of the crude oil was not immediately identified.</p>
<p>Iraq is allowed to sell $2 billion of crude over a six-month period, mainly to buy food and medicine for civilians suffering from sanctions slapped on Baghdad after it invaded Kuwait in 1990.</p>
<p>((--Patrick Connole, New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1828))</p>
